an accused child killer grabs a homicide  detective's gun  new video first obtained by the i-team  shows how that situation  could have turned deadly thank you for  joining us at six i'm brian loftis and  i'm denise valdez the i-team has been  leading coverage on this tragic story  vanessa murphy is here with more on  evidence at the center of the case and  vanessa this video landed terrell rhodes  with even more charges right  yeah terrell rhodes faces a murder  charge and now additional charges  including attempted murder  after he grabbed the homicide  detective's gun  metro police say he had just confessed  to killing two-year-old amari nicholson  he likely knew he was headed to jail  this is terrell rhodes inside an  interview room  one hand is cuffed to the table he tries  to slip his hand  out metro police say he had just  admitted to beating amari nicholson to  death  and burying his body and he drew this  map  to show where  detectives come back in the room to calm  him down  and he pulls the gun from detective opal  deeds holster  she and another detective struggled to  get the loaded firearm back  two other officers entered the room  about a minute after he took the gun  rhodes appears to be restrained  the next day may 12 investigators found  amari's body near paradise and twain  the i-team obtained photos presented to  the grand jury as evidence  one which we've chosen not to air shows  that the toddler was buried in his  footsie pajamas  this photo shows exactly where amari's  remains were found  this was after a community search for  amari for a week  rhodes previously claimed to eight news  now that a mystery woman  took the child while his girlfriend  amari's mother was  out of town what's really sickening is  that people is  making assumptions thinking that i have  something to do with it that  i have heard  manipulated in some way the 27 year old  has since declined the i-team's request  for an interview grab the cop's gun will  you relax  the i-team has learned that metro policy  allows  officers to be armed in an interview  room when there are  two or more officers present the  department also tells me the critical  incident review team is examining the  incident with a focus on  policy tactics and training the findings  will be used to evaluate current  processes and make  future recommendations the head of the  police union also sent me a statement  saying  this shows officers do everything they  can to preserve a life  and highlights the lengths suspects are  willing to go  his full statement at eight newsnow dot  com
 

